  abstract = {We present an observation of photon-photon production of \$τ\$ lepton pairs in ultraperipheral lead-lead collisions. The measurement is based on a data sample with an integrated luminosity of 404 \$μ\$b\$\textasciicircum\{-1\}\$ collected by the CMS experiment at a nucleon-nucleon center-of-mass energy of 5.02 TeV. The \$γγ\$ \$\textbackslash to\$ \$τ\textasciicircum +τ\textasciicircum -\$ process is observed for \$ττ\$ events with a muon and three charged hadrons in the final state. The measured fiducial cross section is \$σ(γγ\$ \$\textbackslash to\$ \$τ\textasciicircum +τ\textasciicircum -)\$ = 4.8 \$\textbackslash pm\$ 0.6 (stat) \$\textbackslash pm\$ 0.5 (syst) \$μ\$b, in agreement with leading-order QED predictions. Using \$σ(γγ\$ \$\textbackslash to\$ \$τ\textasciicircum +τ\textasciicircum -)\$, we estimate a model-dependent value of the anomalous magnetic moment of the \$τ\$ lepton of \$a\_τ\$ = 0.001 \$\textasciicircum\{+0.055\}\_\{-0.089\}\$.},
